WEBVTT

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:27.850
<i>The time is one hundred years ago.</i>

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:31.820
<i>Jean and Nadia escaped from the mighty submarine Nautilus</i>

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:33.230
<i>when it was sinking.</i>

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:36.650
<i>With Marie and King, they washed up on a desert island.</i>

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.030
<i>The children began life on that island all alone.</i>

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:43.750
<i>They found themselves growing up day by day.</i>

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.330
<i>Nadia began to trust Jean because of his devotion,</i>

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:54.420
<i>and she kissed him for the first time and then again.</i>

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.880
<i>She has also grown up mentally,</i>

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:00.970
<i>learning that a friend in need</i>

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:03.140
<i>is truly a friend indeed.</i>

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:07.890
<i>Just as things were looking up,</i>

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:11.810
<i>a terrible typhoon hit the island,</i>

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:14.900
<i>and blew away their peace and civilization.</i>

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.200
<i>But fortune's wheel is always turning,</i>

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:24.490
<i>and Mother Nature presented a huge island before them.</i>

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:30.290
<i>They found Grandis and the others on the new island,</i>

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:34.380
<i>and began living peacefully on the floating island.</i>

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:40.430
<i>But Nadia's fate is not so easy.</i>

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:45.010
<i>Jean and Nadia discovered a large cave</i>

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:50.770
<i>containing a structure just like the Nautilus.</i>

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:54.570
<i>Jean learned that the moving island was artificial.</i>

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:59.320
<i>In the cavern, Nadia was told by a mysterious alien</i>

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.490
<i>that she was not a human being.</i>

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.910
<i>She was very shocked.</i>

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.870
<i>Suddenly, the island began to sink.</i>

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:11.370
<i>Grandis and the rest began their escape on the Gratan.</i>

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:19.220
<i>Jean arrived just in time to help Nadia escape.</i>

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.470
<i>Now that they have lost their peaceful place to live,</i>

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:25.010
<i>they have set sail for the African continent.</i>

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:29.270
<i>It seems that Nadia is just as before.</i>

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:30.770
<i>However...</i>

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:37.400
What's that?

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:42.820
A Garfish!

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.280
A Garfish?

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:47.030
That's Gargoyle's submarine.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:50.710
A submarine? How lucky!

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:52.670
Let's ask them to help us!

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:55.290
Ahoy!

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:59.090
Help us! Ahoy!

00:03:59.090 --> 00:03:59.760
We're...

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.010
You idiot!

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:04.050
What are you doing? They'll find us!

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:08.010
I'm trying to be found! Do you want to stay lost?

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.970
Shut up, you idiot!

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:13.480
What did you say? Withdraw those words!

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:16.980
You moron! That submarine belongs to Gargoyle!

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:20.230
We've been fighting against them.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:22.240
They have their eye on Nadia.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.700
What?

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:26.450
They'll kill us if they find us.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:30.910
Sanson!

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:35.630
We'll win the game by making the first move.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.630
Go to hell!

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:46.140
Amazing!

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:47.510
What happened?

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:50.850
It's obvious! I sunk it with my shot!

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:55.770
No, it must be chasing the sunken island.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.360
How do you know that?

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.320
My sixth sense!

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.160
But why?

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:15.620
Why did Gargoyle's submarine appear there?

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:19.630
And the island sank suddenly.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:23.460
We could see something on the ground while it was sinking.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.300
What happened there, Jean?

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:33.980
Nadia is still sleeping. Will you tell us about it?

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:39.020
There are so many things we don't understand.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:42.190
A lot of things have happened since we met.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:44.530
Gargoyle...

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.070
The Tower of Babel...

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:48.610
The minefield...

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:50.410
The crab robot...

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:51.990
The valley of ancient fish...

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.540
The ruins of Atlantis...

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.200
The giant nautilus...

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.290
The base in Antarctica...

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.210
The space battleship...

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:01.670
Each one by itself was unbelievable.

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:06.630
Nobody will believe all the things we've seen.

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:08.050
That's true.

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:11.050
I would think those things could never have happened.

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:17.100
Come on, what are you talking about? You're all liars.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.020
How nice!

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:24.440
The greatest braggart in the world just called us liars.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:28.700
There are lots of things we wouldn't have believed

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.740
if we hadn't seen them ourselves.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.660
So?

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:38.370
So, the things I saw on that island are also unbelievable.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:41.250
But an island sank.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:44.300
What could be more unbelievable?

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:50.800
I'll tell you everything some other time.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:10.530
Nadia?

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:20.120
You can't sleep?

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:26.210
We'll be in Africa soon.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:27.090
I know.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.010
You don't look so pleased.

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:34.510
No, that's not true.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:38.270
You've been wanting to go to Africa for so long.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:42.690
I wish I could have taken you there in my own invention.

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:44.360
It doesn't matter.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:47.690
We are able to go to Africa because you fixed the Gratan.

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:50.150
Thank you, Jean.

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:54.160
But, Nadia...

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:59.080
What happened beyond that wall?

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:11.010
What's that?

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:13.130
The space battleship!

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:16.640
We've got trouble! Wake up, everybody!

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:20.600
What is it? It's after midnight!

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:21.980
It's the space battleship!

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:25.650
What? First a Garfish, now the space battleship?

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:29.360
Is it my turn again?

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:37.530
Oh, my God!

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:45.920
Somebody, save us!

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:54.630
I see! The gas is rushing out the hole made in the balloon, giving us speed.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:58.050
How lucky! We'll get to Africa sooner,

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:00.260
though it won't be a comfortable ride.

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:04.100
But we can't control our speed this way!

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:08.190
It means we're going to crash someplace going at this speed!

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.400
I can't take this!

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:27.210
I thought I was going to die.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:29.630
My Gratan is indeed great!

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:31.550
There's not a scratch on it!

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:33.710
Where in the world are we?

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:37.220
It must be Heaven.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:43.720
God and the angels must be waiting beyond this hull.

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:47.690
If I just open this hatch...

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:01.120
Jambo?

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:14.590
Jambo!

00:10:14.590 --> 00:10:17.720
Oh my, who does he think he is?

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:19.390
A God or a king?

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:22.100
He thinks he's something all right.

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:25.430
Amazing, Ayerton! You can understand what they say?

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:27.060
Of course!

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:29.190
To tell you the truth,

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:31.900
I was an honorary professor at Cambridge University.

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:33.940
I majored in linguistics!

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:35.360
Jambo!

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:37.400
Is that true?

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:38.900
Why do you ask?

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:41.410
He just keeps saying "jambo".

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:44.950
Jambo! Jambo! Jambo!

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:50.620
Hey, Professor, where are they taking us?

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:55.210
They say they welcome us as honored guests!

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:05.680
This isn't what you told us!

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:10.770
What does he say?

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:14.230
He talks too fast to understand.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:17.740
You lied to us again! You fraud!

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:20.820
This isn't Africa!

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:23.990
It's totally different from what I imagined.

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:26.080
What will happen to us?

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.160
It's this idiot's fault.

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:32.920
Is my life going to end this way?

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:01.320
Is he going to use that?

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:02.570
How cruel!

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:04.410
Say something!

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:06.830
Jambo...

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:11.000
Is that all you can say? You really are a fraud!

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:24.800
Where did you get this?

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:27.510
What? He speaks our language!

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:30.520
What is your name?

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:33.730
Nadia.

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:41.490
Nadia?

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:45.570
What's happening here?

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:47.780
Are they friends?

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:55.790
I don't know what happened,

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:58.170
but I don't think they'll kill us.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:00.000
Where is Nadia?

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:05.970
She's with Hamahama, I imagine.

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:09.430
What are they doing?

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:15.350
S- S- She's probably trying to find out where her native land is.

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:19.060
There's nothing to worry about.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:22.030
You look extremely worried though.

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:32.370
Were you born in this village?

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:36.540
Yes, I was born and brought up in this village.

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:40.500
When is your birthday?

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:42.420
Birthday?

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:48.590
I was born sometime in January, 1877.

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:53.140
I envy you, Hamahama.

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:57.440
I don't know where or when I was born.

00:13:57.640 --> 00:14:00.650
I'm very sorry.

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:04.570
I'm looking for the place where I was born.

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:09.240
It must be somewhere under this wide sky.

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:15.040
Where has she gone?

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:19.540
Isn't she back yet?

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:23.380
I see.

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:27.170
What a poor boy!

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:30.760
Doing that is too cruel.

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:33.220
It's not that bad.

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:37.560
Nadia's grown up enough to fall in love at first sight.

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:40.060
But that's not good!

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:44.190
You're a girl who fell in love at first sight,

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:46.530
and suffered a tragic result.

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:50.950
You mean the Senorita's fake marriage?

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:51.990
You were swindled?

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:53.660
Oh, be quiet!

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:57.870
Don't make fun of the sweet memory of my youth!

00:14:57.870 --> 00:15:01.880
You've really become mild.

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:04.630
You used to say "Shut up!"

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:09.380
And "I'll kill you!" And other things like that.

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:13.300
Once safe on shore, we pray no more.

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:18.350
Anyway, it doesn't matter. It's but a beautiful memory.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:19.890
A beautiful memory?

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:24.310
This is our guardian god, Shisa Shisa.

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:28.320
Shisa Shisa? It looks just like King.

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:33.160
My father told me that the blue stone you have

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:37.290
looks like the one the ruler of the Silver Kingdom had.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:38.750
The Silver Kingdom?

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:40.830
A long time ago, beyond this village,

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:43.130
there was a kingdom made of silver.

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:47.750
But when I was still a child, a big war took place

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:49.720
and the kingdom was destroyed.

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:54.890
A silver column that the king of the Silver kingdom gave us

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:57.510
as a token of friendship is in here.

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:05.520
Evil people from Europe, America, Arabia, and others

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:11.610
have attacked our village trying to take the column.

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:17.450
But we're a people who've never been defeated.

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:19.830
Because we are protected by Shisa Shisa,

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:23.580
the evil ones are no match for us.

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:25.540
That's wonderful.

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:30.800
It's not us. We just do what we must.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:34.720
By the way, we must apologize for how rude we were to you.

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:38.810
We thought you had come to take our column too.

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:44.270
No, that's okay. I'm an evil girl compared with you.

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:48.520
A pretty girl like you could never be evil.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:50.820
Oh, no!

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:57.240
My, you flatter me so charmingly!

00:16:57.490 --> 00:17:03.710
No, it's the truth. We are a people who never lie.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:06.920
Oh, really? Well...

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:11.090
Oh, no! What am I doing?

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:15.260
What's this?

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:20.680
The rightful heir of the Toris Megistos

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:24.430
will see the beginning of human life.

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:28.810
His power will bring destruction to every human

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.440
three times over,

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:35.150
and the light of Babel will incinerate every city.

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:38.740
Nadia, you can read these words?

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:46.160
You really are from Tartessos.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:49.130
Do you know something about Tartessos?

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:52.090
Yes, I do.

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:54.130
Please, tell me about it!

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:55.550
I...

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:57.510
Nadia...

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:10.520
Cheer up, Jean!

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:12.980
Females make up half of the human race.

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:14.940
You'll have lots of chances.

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:21.450
I'd rather be with a machine than a girl anyway.

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:26.120
I like machines. They don't complain.

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:29.960
You can remodel them if you have the technique.

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:32.920
You can't do that to girls.

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:34.500
What?

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:38.720
You're saying the town where you were born is near here?

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:42.180
Yes, Hamahama told me so.

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:43.890
How nice for you!

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:48.310
And Hamahama is such a nice boy.

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:50.480
Hey, have you seen King anywhere?

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:52.190
King?

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:53.980
I haven't seen him for a while.

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:56.150
Where could he have gone?

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:25.430
Did you find him?

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:26.350
No.

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:27.140
Not anywhere.

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:29.770
Did he run away from home again?

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:31.230
Again?

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:34.650
Yes, King is a very jealous lion.

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:39.030
He ran away once when he saw Jean and Nadia kissing.

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:40.450
Kissing?

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:44.830
She shouldn't have changed her mind if she did that.

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:46.540
She's too cruel!

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:48.580
Keep this a secret, okay?

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:56.800
What did you say?

00:19:57.090 --> 00:20:02.010
King is missing. Will you search for him with me?

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:05.970
King is the name of the lion you were with, right?

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:09.430
Yes, I'm so worried about him!

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:12.730
That's terrible. Let's go find him!

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:16.360
It's a terrible sight to see.

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:19.610
Marie will go and tell Jean about this.

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:22.070
Why are you going to do that?

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:24.700
I feel sorry for Jean.

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:27.280
So, I'm going to give him a chance.

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:02.820
King is lost?

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:05.530
Please, Jean, help me find him.

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:07.780
Sure, but...

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:11.080
King!

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:16.080
Where are you going?

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:25.720
Why do we have to run after we've made it to Africa?

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:28.010
Yeah! Where's the Gratan?

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:31.060
The engine isn't working very well.

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:35.140
Why is it always useless when we need it the most?

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:38.520
I didn't know King could run so fast.

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:41.730
Could he have drunk the red fruit juice?

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:43.940
Red fruit juice?

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:47.950
It's a secret medicine handed down in our village.

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:51.160
By taking it, we gain a strange magical power.

00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:11.680
What a cute lion!

00:22:11.970 --> 00:22:14.930
What a poor lion!

00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:18.520
Well, well, how unusual.

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:20.650
It's a white lion cub.

00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:26.780
King!

00:22:28.240 --> 00:22:30.240
King! King!

00:22:32.950 --> 00:22:34.740
Everyone, get down!

00:22:39.370 --> 00:22:40.790
What's that?

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:44.840
They have an eye on our treasure.

00:22:44.840 --> 00:22:45.670
Treasure?

00:22:45.670 --> 00:22:49.720
We thought we'd beaten them. Why are they still here?

00:22:50.760 --> 00:22:58.390
Hamahama! Is that you Hamahama, hiding out there?

00:22:58.690 --> 00:23:01.310
How does he know we're here?

00:23:05.650 --> 00:23:11.280
Is this the one you're looking for, Hamahama?

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:16.120
King!

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:18.460
Well, Hamahama?

00:23:18.460 --> 00:23:25.090
I think the time has come to settle our problem quietly. Don't you agree?

00:23:25.630 --> 00:23:29.800
Shut up! I don't like your roundabout way of talking!

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:31.890
Very well, I'll give it to you straight then.

00:23:32.590 --> 00:23:34.600
If you want this lion to remain alive,

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:39.560
you must give us your treasure.

00:23:39.770 --> 00:23:42.310
I'll give you twenty-four hours.

00:23:42.310 --> 00:23:44.060
If you don't answer by then,

00:23:44.610 --> 00:23:49.280
I'll execute this lion cub!
